      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <math.h>\n\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\n\n/*\n * Each body holds coordinate positions (i.e., x, y, and z) and\n * velocities (i.e., vx, vy, and vz).\n */\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\n\n/*\n * Compute the gravitational impact among all pairs of bodies in \n * the system.\n * Uses 2D tiling (i-loop and j-loop) to improve cache reuse while\n * preserving exact floating-point operation order per body.\n */\nvoid body_force(Body *restrict p, float dt, int n) {\n    // Allocate temporary force accumulators for all bodies\n    float *fx = (float*)malloc(n * sizeof(float));\n    float *fy = (float*)malloc(n * sizeof(float));\n    float *fz = (float*)malloc(n * sizeof(float));\n    if (!fx || !fy || !fz) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"Memory allocation failed\\n\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    // Initialize force accumulators to zero\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        fx[i] = 0.0f;\n        fy[i] = 0.0f;\n        fz[i] = 0.0f;\n    }\n\n    // Tile sizes chosen to fit in L1 cache (ARM64: ~32-64KB)\n    const int BI = 128;   // i-tile size\n    const int BJ = 256;   // j-tile size\n\n    for (int ii = 0; ii < n; ii += BI) {\n        int imax = ii + BI;\n        if (imax > n) imax = n;\n\n        for (int jj = 0; jj < n; jj += BJ) {\n            int jmax = jj + BJ;\n            if (jmax > n) jmax = n;\n\n            // Process one tile: compute forces between bodies in [ii,imax)\n            // and bodies in [jj,jmax).\n            for (int i = ii; i < imax; ++i) {\n                float xi = p[i].x;\n                float yi = p[i].y;\n                float zi = p[i].z;\n\n                float fxi = fx[i];\n                float fyi = fy[i];\n                float fzi = fz[i];\n\n                for (int j = jj; j < jmax; ++j) {\n                    float dx = p[j].x - xi;\n                    float dy = p[j].y - yi;\n                    float dz = p[j].z - zi;\n                    float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\n                    float inv_dist = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\n                    float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n\n                    fxi += dx * inv_dist3;\n                    fyi += dy * inv_dist3;\n                    fzi += dz * inv_dist3;\n                }\n\n                fx[i] = fxi;\n                fy[i] = fyi;\n                fz[i] = fzi;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Update velocities using accumulated forces\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        p[i].vx += dt * fx[i];\n        p[i].vy += dt * fy[i];\n        p[i].vz += dt * fz[i];\n    }\n\n    free(fx);\n    free(fy);\n    free(fz);\n}\n\n/*\n * Read a binary dataset with initilized bodies.\n */\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading nbodie value\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n  Body *bodies = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\n  b = fread(bodies, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading input values\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n\n  return bodies;\n}\n\n/*\n * Write simulation results into a binary dataset.\n */\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\n  int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError writing to output\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n}\n\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\n  int nbodies;\n\n  Body *bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\n\n  /*\n   * At each simulation iteration, interbody forces are computed,\n   * and bodies' positions are integrated.\n   */\n  for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; iter++) {\n    body_force(bodies, DT, nbodies);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; i++) {\n      bodies[i].x += bodies[i].vx * DT;\n      bodies[i].y += bodies[i].vy * DT;\n      bodies[i].z += bodies[i].vz * DT;\n    }\n  }\n\n  write_dataset(nbodies, bodies);\n\n  free(bodies);\n  \n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/nbody.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Tiling both i and j loops in the force computation improves cache reuse by processing blocks of bodies together, keeping frequently accessed data in L1 cache. The exact order of floating-point additions per body is preserved because contributions from each j-block are accumulated sequentially across tiles, ensuring bitwise identical output.",
  "notes": "Applied 2D tiling with BI=128 and BJ=256 to the force computation loop. Temporary force arrays (fx,fy,fz) accumulate contributions for all bodies; after processing all tiles, velocities are updated. The inner j-loop order remains increasing within each tile, so per-body addition sequence matches the original code exactly.",
